    "32-year-old man with newly diagnosed diabetes mellitus, recently diagnosed hyperlipidemia, hypertension, mood disorders, and methamphetamine use in remission presented with palpitations and constant right-sided chest wall pain for two days.",
    "He denied abdominal pain and had no abdominal tenderness, distension, guarding, or rigidity.",
    "He was tachycardic and tachypneic with WBC 16.4 x 10^3/uL and normal lactic acid; DKA labs included glucose 356 mg/dL, anion gap 24 mEq/L, bicarbonate 7 mEq/L, pH 7.17, 2+ urine ketones, and HbA1c greater than 17.6%.",
    "Lipid testing showed triglycerides 2172 mg/dL, cholesterol 351 mg/dL, HDL 14 mg/dL, and lipase 472 U/L.",
    "CT later showed diffuse peripancreatic edema compatible with acute pancreatitis; triglycerides fell below 500 mg/dL after two days of NPO status, insulin drip, and IV fluids."
